From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MicroNUX <micronux@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 23:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] video: fbdev: contain ESP32-P4 display faults safely

Never illuminate the panel unless a verified framebuffer or VPG source is
active and healthy. Track the last confirmed hardware brightness, preserve
a valid video producer when backlight I2C completion is ambiguous, and mark
scanout inactive after every destructive stop attempt.

Latch DMA errors, bridge underruns, stale frames, and fatal DSI payload
faults in IRQ-safe paths, then turn the backlight off from process context
without disturbing the last source. Serialize and retain the DSI host's
read-to-clear status registers for post-fault evidence.

Do not infer producer death from one aged DMA interrupt timestamp. USB
endpoint activity can delay interrupt service while GDMA keeps scanning.
Poll every 50 ms and require six executed samples with both the completed
frame count and live source address stationary. Missed callbacks count only
once, while either hardware-progress signal prevents false containment.

Darken and settle before every bounded VPG source transition, discard only
the intentional dark transition residue, prime the selected source before
reveal, and keep the health timer stopped until framebuffer restoration is
validated. Require reboot after destructive faults because Linux does not
yet own a proven panel reinitialization sequence. Close IRQ, workqueue, and
backlight lifetimes before releasing framebuffer-private state.

Signed-off-by: MicroNUX <micronux@example.invalid>
